# L §6.4, §8.3 (tally 2.1.6, issue #75): the base is whole without its scenarios, so a base ask that reads extra,
# a def only the scenario's file declares, refuses the reality at load, LOAD-SCENARIO `<item> of scenario <s> is
# read outside it`, whatever the asks (here q, which reads doubled). tally 2.1.5's refcore read extra as a key
# literal and refused only an ask that reached it, at run (LOAD-KEY ambiguous key extra). T's held
# scen/scenario-read; the engine's bytes.
=== model.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented): a model and a scenario over it, scen.tally; it loads clean"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money PLN

def doubled: money PLN = amt + amt at reader

ask q: doubled law 2026-03-01

ask q2: extra law 2027-06-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
=== scen.tally
scenario raised over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version raise_2027
  cite card
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-02-01
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "a raise from 2027"

ask q_raised: doubled in raised law 2027-06-01

def extra: money PLN = amt at reader
=== expect q
refused: LOAD-SCENARIO extra of scenario raised is read outside it (model.tally:18)
